IMPORT prelude

-- Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) -- Part IX, debt agreements, from the debtor's seat: may I give a debt agreement proposal
-- (s 185C(1), (4), (4A), (4C), (5), with s 5(2)-(3) "insolvent"); how long may my payments run (s 185C(2AA)-(2AC)); what may the
-- Official Receiver do with my proposal (s 185E(2), (2AA), (2AB), (3)); the applicable deadline (s 185); the creditors' vote and lapse
-- (ss 185EC, 185G(b)); when my agreement is made (s 185H); what my creditors may do to me while it is processed and while it is in
-- force (ss 185F, 185K); whether a creditor may petition to make me bankrupt (ss 40(1)(g), (ha)-(hd), 44(1), 185K(1)); what each
-- creditor gets (s 185C(2)(d), (e)); arrears defaults and termination (ss 185LB(3), 185LC(3), 185QA, 185R); how far a variation may
-- extend my payments (s 185M(1D)-(1DB)); the end of my agreement and my release (ss 185N(1), (2), 185NA, with s 153(2)); how long it
-- stays on the National Personal Insolvency Index (Bankruptcy Regulations 2021 ss 82, 83); and how long it bars another proposal
-- (s 185C(4)(a)).
--
-- SEAT: the debtor -- "May I propose a debt agreement instead of bankruptcy; what does it bind me to, and when am I released?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 97, compilation date 21 May 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 47, 2026), Federal Register of
-- Legislation register id C2026C00215, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1966A00033.txt. Regulations: Bankruptcy
-- Regulations 2021, Compilation No. 5, compilation date 1 July 2026 (register id F2026C00537), as deposited at
-- ../../../bankruptcy-regulations-2021/registers/source-bundle/F2021L00261.txt -- s 10A (the statutory minimum, $10,000) and
-- ss 82, 83 (removal from the Index). The Regulations prescribe no greater amount for s 185C(4)(b)(ii). The s 185C(4)(e) and
-- s 185M(1E) formulas, images the text deposit lost, are taken from ../../registers/source-bundle/C1966A00033.formulas.md
-- (transcribed by hand on 21 October 2026 from the Word rendering of the same compilation).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the threshold amount itself (7 times a Social Security Act 1991 rate that is indexed), an INPUT; the Minister's
-- s 185C(4B) percentage and low income debtor amount, which the formulas use, are INPUTS (the instrument is not deposited); approved forms, the statement of affairs (s 185D) and explanatory
-- statement; cancellation of acceptance (s 185ED); voting on variations and terminations (ss 185MA-185PD); termination and voiding
-- by the Court (ss 185Q, 185T-185V) beyond their effect on the Index; s 185EC(3) (debts assigned to a related entity); administrators'
-- duties, registration and remuneration beyond what reaches the debtor; Part X; the credit file (Privacy Act 1988 Part IIIA).
-- Bankruptcy itself is in bda-bankruptcy.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied, with the
-- design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use
-- as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bankruptcy Act 1966 Part IX -- debt agreements, from the debtor's seat`

§§ `helpers`

-- A date is given as year, month and day and compared by a single key (YYYYMMDD).
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`date key` MEANS `year` TIMES 10000 PLUS `month` TIMES 100 PLUS `day`

GIVEN `first amount` IS A NUMBER, `second amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS
    IF `first amount` GREATER THAN `second amount` THEN `first amount` ELSE `second amount`

-- The same day N years later, as a key. (A 29 February start is not handled.)
GIVEN `a date` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the same day years later` MEANS `a date` PLUS `years` TIMES 10000

-- "N years beginning on the day the agreement is made" ends at the end of the day before the Nth anniversary, so a payment falls
-- after that period if it is due on or after the anniversary. (Inference from the words.)
GIVEN `made` IS A NUMBER, `last payment` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the last payment falls after the period of years` IF
    `last payment` AT LEAST `the same day years later` `made` `years`

§§ `185C(2AB) -- my home`

-- s 185C(2AB): applies "if at the time the debtor gives the debt agreement proposal ... the debtor has an interest in real property
-- in Australia that is a dwelling and is the debtor's principal place of residence, being an interest: (a) that is an interest under
-- a long-term lease; or (b) that is any other legal or equitable estate or interest, except: (i) an interest under a lease (other
-- than a long-term lease); or (ii) an interest under a licence; or (iii) a life interest; or (iv) an interest in an easement; or (v)
-- an interest held on trust for another person; or (vi) an interest of a kind determined in an instrument under subsection (2AD)".
-- s 185C(5): "long-term lease" -- a lease granted by the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory for a term "reasonably likely ... to
-- exceed 20 years"; "lease includes a sublease".
DECLARE `Home interest` IS ONE OF
    `no interest in a dwelling`
    `a lease other than a long-term lease`
    `a long-term lease`
    `a licence`
    `a life interest`
    `an interest in an easement`
    `an interest held on trust for another person`
    `a kind determined by the Minister's instrument`
    `any other legal or equitable estate or interest`

@export Does the home rule in s 185C(2AB) apply to me (which lets my payments run up to 5 years)?
GIVEN `my interest` IS A `Home interest` @desc The kind of interest you hold in the home you live in (a rented home is "a lease other than a long-term lease"; a home you own is "any other legal or equitable estate or interest")
      `it is my principal place of residence in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that home is a dwelling in Australia and your principal place of residence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the home rule apply to me` IF
        `it is my principal place of residence in Australia`
    AND CONSIDER `my interest`
        WHEN `a long-term lease` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other legal or equitable estate or interest` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `185C(1), (4), (4A), (4C), (5) -- may I give a proposal`

-- s 185C(1): "A debtor who is insolvent may give the Official Receiver a written proposal for a debt agreement." s 5(3): "A person
-- who is not solvent is insolvent"; s 5(2): solvent "if, and only if, the person is able to pay all the person's debts, as and when
-- they become due and payable".
-- s 185C(4): a debtor "cannot" give a proposal if (a) "at any time in the 10 years immediately before the proposal time" the debtor
-- "(i) has been a bankrupt; or (ii) has been a party (as debtor) to a debt agreement; or (iii) has given an authority under section
-- 188"; (b) unsecured debts "total more than (i) the threshold amount; or (ii) if the regulations prescribe a greater amount ... the
-- amount prescribed" (the 2021 Regulations prescribe none); (c) divisible property "is more than twice the threshold amount"; (d)
-- after tax income in the year beginning at the proposal time "is likely to exceed three-quarters of the threshold amount"; (e) if
-- (2AB) does not apply, the formula percentage exceeds the Minister's percentage "(unless subsection (4C) applies to the debtor)".
-- (4A): (a)(i) does not apply to a bankruptcy "annulled under section 153B". (4C): applies if the formula exceeds and the proposed
-- administrator certifies the debtor "is likely to be able to discharge the obligations created by the agreement as and when they
-- fall due". s 185C(2E): "A debt agreement proposal must not be given jointly by 2 or more debtors."
-- s 185C(5): "threshold amount ... means 7 times the amount that, at that time, is specified in column 3, item 2, Table B, point
-- 1064-B1, Pension Rate Calculator A, in the Social Security Act 1991"; "unsecured debt includes the amount by which the value of a
-- debt exceeds the value of a security given for the debt"; "after tax income" -- likely taxable income less income tax and the
-- Medicare levy.
-- "Insolvent" is the Act's own term but turns on facts about every debt; it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE Debtor HAS
    `is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a bankrupt in the previous 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that bankruptcy was annulled under s 153B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a party as debtor to a debt agreement in the previous 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave an authority under s 188 in the previous 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unsecured debts` IS A NUMBER
    `property divisible among creditors if bankrupt` IS A NUMBER
    `likely after tax income in the next year` IS A NUMBER
    `interest in the home` IS A `Home interest`
    `the home is a dwelling in Australia and the principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `total of the payments I would be required to make under the agreement` IS A NUMBER
    `the low income debtor amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister's s 185C(4B) percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `the proposed administrator gave a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives the proposal jointly with another debtor` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 185C(4)(e): "the amount worked out using the following formula (expressed as a percentage)". The formula, transcribed in
-- C1966A00033.formulas.md:
--     (Total of the payments that the debtor would be required to make under the agreement + Low income debtor amount
--        (see subsection (5)))
--     / The debtor's after tax income (see subsection (5)) in the year beginning at the proposal time
-- s 185C(5): "low income debtor amount means the amount determined in an instrument under subsection (4B)". Both the amount and
-- the percentage are set by that instrument, which is not deposited: they are inputs.
@export What is my s 185C(4)(e) payments-to-income percentage?
GIVEN `total payments` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the payments you would be required to make under the agreement, in dollars
      `low income debtor amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The low income debtor amount set by the Minister's s 185C(4B) instrument, in dollars
      `after tax income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your after tax income in the year beginning when you give the proposal, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my payments to income percentage` IS
    IF `after tax income` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE (`total payments` PLUS `low income debtor amount`) TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY `after tax income`

-- With no after tax income the formula divides by nothing; any payment then exceeds every percentage (an encoding choice, as
-- the text does not say).
@export Does the s 185C(4)(e) formula exceed the Minister's percentage?
GIVEN `total payments` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the payments you would be required to make under the agreement, in dollars
      `low income debtor amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The low income debtor amount set by the Minister's s 185C(4B) instrument, in dollars
      `after tax income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your after tax income in the year beginning when you give the proposal, in dollars
      `the Minister's percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage set by the Minister's s 185C(4B) instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my payments exceed the Minister's percentage` IF
    IF `after tax income` AT MOST 0
    THEN `total payments` PLUS `low income debtor amount` GREATER THAN 0
    ELSE `What is my payments to income percentage` `total payments` `low income debtor amount` `after tax income`
             GREATER THAN `the Minister's percentage`

GIVEN `the debtor` IS A Debtor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 185C(4)(e) formula exceeds the Minister's percentage` IF
    `Do my payments exceed the Minister's percentage`
        (`the debtor`'s `total of the payments I would be required to make under the agreement`)
        (`the debtor`'s `the low income debtor amount`)
        (`the debtor`'s `likely after tax income in the next year`)
        (`the debtor`'s `the Minister's s 185C(4B) percentage`)

GIVEN `the Social Security Act rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold amount` MEANS 7 TIMES `the Social Security Act rate`

GIVEN `the debtor` IS A Debtor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home rule applies to the debtor` IF
    `Does the home rule apply to me` (`the debtor`'s `interest in the home`) (`the debtor`'s `the home is a dwelling in Australia and the principal place of residence`)

DECLARE Eligibility IS ONE OF
    `I may give a debt agreement proposal`
    `no -- I am not insolvent`
    `no -- I was bankrupt, in a debt agreement or gave a s 188 authority in the last 10 years`
    `no -- my unsecured debts are more than the threshold amount`
    `no -- my divisible property is more than twice the threshold amount`
    `no -- my likely after tax income is more than three-quarters of the threshold amount`
    `no -- my payments would exceed the Minister's percentage of my income`
    `no -- a proposal cannot be given jointly`

@export May I give the Official Receiver a debt agreement proposal, and if not, why not (s 185C(1), (2E), (4))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Debtor @desc Your circumstances at the time you would give the proposal
      `threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The threshold amount at that time, in dollars (7 times the Social Security Act 1991 point 1064-B1 Table B item 2 rate)
GIVETH AN Eligibility
DECIDE `May I give a debt agreement proposal` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `me`'s `is insolvent`
            THEN `no -- I am not insolvent`
        IF     (`me`'s `was a bankrupt in the previous 10 years` AND (NOT `me`'s `that bankruptcy was annulled under s 153B`))
            OR `me`'s `was a party as debtor to a debt agreement in the previous 10 years`
            OR `me`'s `gave an authority under s 188 in the previous 10 years`
            THEN `no -- I was bankrupt, in a debt agreement or gave a s 188 authority in the last 10 years`
        IF `me`'s `unsecured debts` GREATER THAN `threshold`
            THEN `no -- my unsecured debts are more than the threshold amount`
        IF `me`'s `property divisible among creditors if bankrupt` GREATER THAN 2 TIMES `threshold`
            THEN `no -- my divisible property is more than twice the threshold amount`
        IF `me`'s `likely after tax income in the next year` GREATER THAN `threshold` TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 4
            THEN `no -- my likely after tax income is more than three-quarters of the threshold amount`
        IF     (NOT `the home rule applies to the debtor` `me`)
           AND `the s 185C(4)(e) formula exceeds the Minister's percentage` `me`
           AND (NOT `me`'s `the proposed administrator gave a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate`)
            THEN `no -- my payments would exceed the Minister's percentage of my income`
        IF `me`'s `gives the proposal jointly with another debtor`
            THEN `no -- a proposal cannot be given jointly`
        OTHERWISE `I may give a debt agreement proposal`

GIVEN `me` IS A Debtor, `threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am eligible` IF
    `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `me` `threshold` EQUALS `I may give a debt agreement proposal`

-- s 185C(4)(a)(ii), (i): "at any time in the 10 years immediately before the proposal time" the debtor "has been a party (as debtor)
-- to a debt agreement" or "has been a bankrupt". A debtor remains a party until the agreement ends, and a bankrupt until discharge,
-- so the 10 years run from the END of the earlier agreement or bankruptcy, not its start. (Inference from the words.)
@export Does an earlier debt agreement or bankruptcy still bar me from giving a new proposal (s 185C(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the day it ended` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your earlier debt agreement ended or you were discharged from bankruptcy, as YYYYMMDD
      `the day I would give the new proposal` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you would give the new proposal, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an earlier agreement or bankruptcy still bar me` IF
    `the day I would give the new proposal` AT MOST `the same day years later` `the day it ended` 10

§§ `185C(2AA), (2AC) -- how long my payments may run`

-- s 185C(2AA): a proposal "must not provide for the debtor to make payments under the agreement, in respect of provable debts ...,
-- after: (a) 3 years beginning on the day the agreement is made; or (b) if subsection (2AB) applies to the debtor -- 5 years".
-- (2AC): if the payments run after 3 but not after 5 years, the property to be dealt with "must not include any interest covered by
-- subsection (2AB)".
@export What is the longest, in years, my debt agreement payments may run (s 185C(2AA))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Debtor @desc Your circumstances when you give the proposal
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years may my payments run` IS
    IF `the home rule applies to the debtor` `me` THEN 5 ELSE 3

DECLARE Proposal HAS
    `the proposing debtor` IS A Debtor
    `day the agreement would be made` IS A NUMBER
    `day of the last payment` IS A NUMBER
    `the property to be dealt with includes the home interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other requirements of s 185C(2), (2A), (2B), (2D), (2DA) and (2F) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days from signing to giving it to the Official Receiver` IS A NUMBER

@export Does my proposal's payment term comply with s 185C(2AA) and (2AC)?
GIVEN `my proposal` IS A Proposal @desc Your proposal: when the agreement would be made, the last payment, and whether it deals with your home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my payment term comply` IF
        (NOT `the last payment falls after the period of years` (`my proposal`'s `day the agreement would be made`) (`my proposal`'s `day of the last payment`) (`How many years may my payments run` (`my proposal`'s `the proposing debtor`)))
    AND (    (NOT `the last payment falls after the period of years` (`my proposal`'s `day the agreement would be made`) (`my proposal`'s `day of the last payment`) 3)
          OR (NOT `my proposal`'s `the property to be dealt with includes the home interest`))

§§ `185E -- what the Official Receiver may do with my proposal`

-- s 185E(2): the Official Receiver "may accept the proposal for processing if (a) the Official Receiver is satisfied that subsections
-- 185C(2), (2AA), (2AC), (2A), (2B), (2D), (2DA), (2E) and (4) have been complied with; ... (e) ... satisfied that the statement of
-- affairs accompanying the proposal is in order". (2AA): "must not accept ... unless the proposal was given ... within 14 days after
-- the day on which the debtor signed the proposal". (2AB): "may refuse ... if the Official Receiver reasonably believes that
-- complying with the agreement would cause undue hardship to the debtor". (3): "must not accept ... if the Official Receiver thinks
-- that the creditors' interests would be better served by not accepting". (4): the debtor may apply to the Administrative Review
-- Tribunal for review.
-- The Official Receiver's judgments are the Official Receiver's: they are asked as inputs, and the answer is conditional on them.
DECLARE `Processing decision` IS ONE OF
    `the Official Receiver cannot accept it for processing`
    `the Official Receiver must not accept it for processing`
    `the Official Receiver may accept it, or may refuse it for undue hardship`
    `the Official Receiver may accept it for processing`

@export What may the Official Receiver do with my debt agreement proposal (s 185E)?
GIVEN `my proposal` IS A Proposal @desc Your proposal
      `threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The threshold amount at the time, in dollars
      `the Official Receiver is satisfied my statement of affairs is in order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver is satisfied that your statement of affairs is in order
      `the Official Receiver thinks creditors are better served by not accepting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver thinks your creditors' interests would be better served by not accepting the proposal
      `the Official Receiver believes it would cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver reasonably believes complying with the agreement would cause you undue hardship
GIVETH A `Processing decision`
DECIDE `What may the Official Receiver do with my proposal` IS
    BRANCH
        IF     (NOT `I am eligible` (`my proposal`'s `the proposing debtor`) `threshold`)
            OR (NOT `Does my payment term comply` `my proposal`)
            OR (NOT `my proposal`'s `the other requirements of s 185C(2), (2A), (2B), (2D), (2DA) and (2F) are met`)
            OR (NOT `the Official Receiver is satisfied my statement of affairs is in order`)
            THEN `the Official Receiver cannot accept it for processing`
        IF     `my proposal`'s `days from signing to giving it to the Official Receiver` GREATER THAN 14
            OR `the Official Receiver thinks creditors are better served by not accepting`
            THEN `the Official Receiver must not accept it for processing`
        IF `the Official Receiver believes it would cause me undue hardship`
            THEN `the Official Receiver may accept it, or may refuse it for undue hardship`
        OTHERWISE `the Official Receiver may accept it for processing`

§§ `185 -- the applicable deadline`

-- s 185 "applicable deadline: (a) in relation to a debt agreement proposal, means: (i) if Official Receiver accepted the proposal for
-- processing in December -- the end of the 42nd day after the acceptance; or (ii) otherwise -- the end of the 35th day after".
@export How many days after my proposal is accepted for processing do my creditors have to reply (s 185 applicable deadline)?
GIVEN `accepted for processing in December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver accepted your proposal for processing in December
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days do my creditors have to reply` IS
    IF `accepted for processing in December` THEN 42 ELSE 35

§§ `185EC, 185G(b) -- my creditors' vote`

-- s 185EC(1): "A debt agreement proposal is accepted if: (a) the Official Receiver writes to affected creditors ...; and (b) a
-- majority in value of the creditors who reply before the applicable deadline state that the proposal should be accepted." (1A):
-- disregard an affected creditor who "is the proposed administrator" or "was, on becoming an affected creditor, a related entity of
-- the proposed administrator". (2): "taken to be accepted at the applicable deadline". (4): value "assessed as at the time when the
-- acceptance ... for processing was recorded on the National Personal Insolvency Index". (5): "a secured creditor is taken to be a
-- creditor only to the extent (if any) by which the amount of the debt owing to the creditor exceeds the value of the creditor's
-- security".
-- s 185G: the proposal lapses if "(b) the Official Receiver accepts the proposal for processing and writes to affected creditors
-- about it, but no replies are received before the applicable deadline".
-- "Majority" is read as more than half of the value of the counted replies; a tie is not a majority. A reply from a disregarded
-- creditor still prevents a lapse under s 185G(b), which speaks of "no replies" (inference from the words).
DECLARE Creditor HAS
    `debt owing when acceptance for processing was recorded` IS A NUMBER
    `value of the creditor's security` IS A NUMBER
    `is the proposed administrator or was its related entity on becoming a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `replied before the applicable deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stated the proposal should be accepted` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the creditor` IS A Creditor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the creditor` MEANS
    IF `the creditor`'s `debt owing when acceptance for processing was recorded` GREATER THAN `the creditor`'s `value of the creditor's security`
    THEN `the creditor`'s `debt owing when acceptance for processing was recorded` MINUS `the creditor`'s `value of the creditor's security`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the creditor` IS A Creditor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor's reply counts` IF
        `the creditor`'s `replied before the applicable deadline`
    AND (NOT `the creditor`'s `is the proposed administrator or was its related entity on becoming a creditor`)

GIVEN `the creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`value of counted replies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the creditors`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `one creditor` FOLLOWED BY `the others` THEN
        (IF `the creditor's reply counts` `one creditor` THEN `the value of the creditor` `one creditor` ELSE 0)
        PLUS `value of counted replies` `the others`

GIVEN `the creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`value of counted replies in favour` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the creditors`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `one creditor` FOLLOWED BY `the others` THEN
        (IF `the creditor's reply counts` `one creditor` AND `one creditor`'s `stated the proposal should be accepted`
         THEN `the value of the creditor` `one creditor` ELSE 0)
        PLUS `value of counted replies in favour` `the others`

GIVEN `the creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any creditor replied` IF
    CONSIDER `the creditors`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `one creditor` FOLLOWED BY `the others` THEN
        `one creditor`'s `replied before the applicable deadline` OR `any creditor replied` `the others`

DECLARE `Vote outcome` IS ONE OF
    `my proposal is accepted`
    `my proposal is not accepted`
    `my proposal lapses`

@export What happens to my proposal on my creditors' vote (ss 185EC, 185G)?
GIVEN `my creditors` IS A LIST OF Creditor @desc Each affected creditor: the debt owed when acceptance for processing was recorded, any security, whether it is the proposed administrator or its related entity, whether it replied in time, and how it voted
GIVETH A `Vote outcome`
DECIDE `What happens to my proposal on the vote` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `any creditor replied` `my creditors`
            THEN `my proposal lapses`
        IF 2 TIMES `value of counted replies in favour` `my creditors` GREATER THAN `value of counted replies` `my creditors`
            THEN `my proposal is accepted`
        OTHERWISE `my proposal is not accepted`

§§ `185H, 185I -- when my agreement is made, and with whom`

-- s 185H(2): if a proposal is accepted and is not conditional, "the Official Receiver must enter details of the debt agreement ... on
-- the National Personal Insolvency Index; and (d) the debt agreement is made in the terms of the proposal when those details are so
-- entered". (3): a conditional proposal likewise, but only if "the event occurs within that period". s 185C(2F): the period "must not
-- be longer than 7 days". s 185I: the parties are "(a) the debtor; and (b) the creditors to whom the debtor owed provable debts" --
-- including those who voted no or did not reply.
@export Is my debt agreement made (s 185H)?
GIVEN `my proposal was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your creditors accepted the proposal
      `it was conditional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proposal was subject to a specified event within a specified period
      `the event occurred within the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a conditional proposal, whether the event occurred within the period
      `details are entered on the Index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver has entered the agreement's details on the National Personal Insolvency Index
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my debt agreement made` IF
        `my proposal was accepted`
    AND `details are entered on the Index`
    AND ((NOT `it was conditional`) OR `the event occurred within the period`)

@export Is a creditor who voted against my proposal, or did not reply, bound by my debt agreement (s 185I)?
GIVEN `the creditor was owed a provable debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owed that creditor a provable debt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a creditor who voted no bound` IF `the creditor was owed a provable debt`

§§ `185F, 185K -- what my creditors may do to me`

-- s 185 "frozen debt" is a debt owed by a debtor whose proposal has been accepted for processing that "would be a provable debt ...
-- but does not include a debt arising under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order". "provable debt" -- "a debt that would
-- have been provable in bankruptcy if the debtor had become a bankrupt when the acceptance of the relevant debt agreement proposal for
-- processing was recorded in the National Personal Insolvency Index".
-- s 185F(1), from the recording of acceptance for processing until the deadline or the agreement: (a) a creditor cannot "apply for
-- enforcement of, or enforce, a remedy against the debtor's person or property in respect of a frozen debt"; (b) a sheriff must not
-- execute process to enforce payment of a frozen debt; (c) a person entitled to retain or deduct money owing to the debtor "must not
-- retain or deduct money". (2): a creditor may still start a legal proceeding or take a fresh step "(except to enforce a judgment)".
-- (3): proceeds of crime liabilities may be enforced.
-- s 185K(1): while the agreement is in force and on the Index, a creditor cannot (a) present a creditor's petition, (b) proceed with
-- one already presented, or "(c) enforce a remedy against the debtor's person or property, or start or take a fresh step in legal
-- proceedings, in respect of a provable debt". (2): (1)(c) does not prevent enforcing a remedy for "(a) a maintenance agreement; (b)
-- a maintenance order; (c) a proceeds of crime law". (3): "(a) a sheriff must not ... enforce payment of a provable debt ...; and (b)
-- a person who is entitled under a law of the Commonwealth, or of a State or Territory, to retain or deduct money from money that is
-- or will be owing or payable to the debtor must not retain or deduct money."
-- s 185K(3)(b) and s 185F(1)(c) are not limited to any kind of debt; encoded on their words (NOTES.md finding 4).
-- Whether a maintenance or proceeds of crime liability is itself provable is not decided: for the proceedings limbs it is treated as
-- provable (an assumption). A debt incurred after acceptance for processing was recorded is not provable (from the s 185 definition).
DECLARE `Debt kind` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary provable debt`
    `a debt incurred by fraud`
    `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order`
    `a liability under a proceeds of crime law`
    `a debt incurred after acceptance for processing was recorded`

DECLARE `Creditor action` IS ONE OF
    `enforce a remedy against my person or property`
    `start legal proceedings`
    `take a fresh step in proceedings other than to enforce a judgment`
    `have a sheriff execute court process`
    `retain or deduct money owing to me`

GIVEN `the debt` IS A `Debt kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt is provable` IF
    CONSIDER `the debt`
    WHEN `a debt incurred after acceptance for processing was recorded` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the debt` IS A `Debt kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt is frozen` IF
    CONSIDER `the debt`
    WHEN `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a debt incurred after acceptance for processing was recorded` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export While my debt agreement proposal is being processed, may a creditor take this action against me (s 185F)?
GIVEN `the action` IS A `Creditor action` @desc What the creditor wants to do
      `the debt` IS A `Debt kind` @desc The kind of debt it is for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a creditor act against me while my proposal is processed` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `enforce a remedy against my person or property` THEN
            (NOT `the debt is frozen` `the debt`)
         OR (`the debt` EQUALS `a liability under a proceeds of crime law`)
    WHEN `start legal proceedings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `take a fresh step in proceedings other than to enforce a judgment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `have a sheriff execute court process` THEN NOT `the debt is frozen` `the debt`
    WHEN `retain or deduct money owing to me` THEN FALSE

@export While my debt agreement is in force, may a creditor take this action against me (s 185K)?
GIVEN `the action` IS A `Creditor action` @desc What the creditor wants to do
      `the debt` IS A `Debt kind` @desc The kind of debt it is for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a creditor act against me while my agreement is in force` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `enforce a remedy against my person or property` THEN
            (NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`)
         OR (`the debt` EQUALS `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order`)
         OR (`the debt` EQUALS `a liability under a proceeds of crime law`)
    WHEN `start legal proceedings` THEN NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`
    WHEN `take a fresh step in proceedings other than to enforce a judgment` THEN NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`
    WHEN `have a sheriff execute court process` THEN NOT `the debt is provable` `the debt`
    WHEN `retain or deduct money owing to me` THEN FALSE

§§ `40(1), 44(1), 185K(1) -- may a creditor petition to make me bankrupt`

-- s 40(1): a debtor commits an act of bankruptcy "(g)" on failing to comply with a bankruptcy notice served after a final judgment;
-- "(ha) if the debtor gives the Official Receiver a debt agreement proposal; (hb) if a debt agreement proposal given by the debtor
-- ... is accepted by the debtor's creditors; (hc) if the debtor breaches a debt agreement; (hd) if a debt agreement to which the
-- debtor was a party (as a debtor) is terminated under section 185P, 185Q or 185QA".
-- s 44(1): a creditor's petition "shall not be presented" unless (a) the debt or debts owed to the petitioning creditor or creditors
-- "amount to the statutory minimum"; (b) each is "a liquidated sum" payable immediately or at a certain future time; and (c) "the
-- act of bankruptcy on which the petition is founded was committed within 6 months before the presentation of the petition". (2): a
-- secured creditor counts only its shortfall unless it offers to surrender its security (3).
-- s 5(1) "statutory minimum means: (a) if an amount greater than $5,000 is prescribed -- the prescribed amount; or (b) otherwise --
-- $5,000"; Bankruptcy Regulations 2021 s 10A: "the amount prescribed is $10,000".
-- s 185K(1)(a), (b): while the agreement is in force and on the Index a creditor cannot present or proceed with a petition.
-- s 185F does not stop a petition while the proposal is being processed, and giving the proposal is itself an act of bankruptcy.
-- Whether the Court then makes a sequestration order (s 43, s 52) is the Court's and is not encoded.
DECLARE `Act of bankruptcy` IS ONE OF
    `failing to comply with a bankruptcy notice`
    `giving a debt agreement proposal`
    `my creditors accepting my debt agreement proposal`
    `breaching my debt agreement`
    `my debt agreement being terminated under s 185P, 185Q or 185QA`
    `no act of bankruptcy`

-- s 5(1) "statutory minimum", with Bankruptcy Regulations 2021 s 10A.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory minimum` MEANS `the higher of` 5000 10000

@export May a creditor present a bankruptcy petition against me (ss 40, 44(1), 185K(1))?
GIVEN `the act` IS AN `Act of bankruptcy` @desc The act of bankruptcy the creditor relies on
      `months since the act` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months before the petition the act of bankruptcy happened
      `liquidated debts owed to the petitioning creditors` IS A NUMBER @desc The liquidated, unsecured debts you owe to the creditor or creditors petitioning, in dollars
      `my debt agreement is in force and on the Index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a debt agreement in force and entered on the National Personal Insolvency Index
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a creditor petition to make me bankrupt` IF
        (NOT `my debt agreement is in force and on the Index`)
    AND (NOT `the act` EQUALS `no act of bankruptcy`)
    AND `months since the act` AT MOST 6
    AND `liquidated debts owed to the petitioning creditors` AT LEAST `the statutory minimum`

§§ `185C(2)(d), (e) -- what each creditor gets`

-- s 185C(2)(d): the proposal must provide that "all provable debts ... rank equally" and, if the total paid "is insufficient to meet
-- those provable debts in full, those provable debts are to be paid proportionately"; (e) "a creditor is not entitled to receive, in
-- respect of a provable debt, more than the amount of the debt". The administrator's remuneration (s 185C(3A)) is paid in addition
-- and is not modelled.
@export How much will this creditor receive under my debt agreement (s 185C(2)(d), (e))?
GIVEN `this creditor's provable debt` IS A NUMBER @desc The provable debt you owe this creditor, in dollars
      `all provable debts` IS A NUMBER @desc All provable debts under the agreement, in dollars
      `total I pay towards provable debts` IS A NUMBER @desc The total you will pay under the agreement towards provable debts (not the administrator's fee), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will this creditor receive` IS
    IF `total I pay towards provable debts` AT LEAST `all provable debts`
    THEN `this creditor's provable debt`
    ELSE `total I pay towards provable debts` TIMES `this creditor's provable debt` DIVIDED BY `all provable debts`

§§ `185LB(3), 185LC(3), 185QA, 185R -- if I fall behind`

-- s 185LB(3): a 3-month arrears default occurs at the test time if (a) payments became due at the start of the 3-month period ending
-- immediately before it; (b) "throughout that 3-month period, the debtor was in arrears"; and (c) "(i) the total amount that the
-- debtor was so in arrears exceeds $300, or 20% of the total of all of the due payments at the beginning of that 3-month period,
-- whichever is higher; or (ii) if the total of all of the due payments at the beginning of that 3-month period was $300 or less -- no
-- payment was made in that period to reduce any of the due payments". (1): the administrator must notify each creditor within 10
-- business days. The default does not by itself end the agreement.
@export Have I committed a 3-month arrears default, so that my creditors must be told (s 185LB)?
GIVEN `in arrears throughout the 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were behind throughout the 3 months
      `total arrears` IS A NUMBER @desc How much you are behind, in dollars
      `total due at the start of the 3 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the payments that were due at the start of the 3 months, in dollars
      `I made a payment in the period to reduce them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid anything in the 3 months to reduce the arrears
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed a 3-month arrears default` IF
        `in arrears throughout the 3 months`
    AND (    `total arrears` GREATER THAN `the higher of` 300 (`total due at the start of the 3 months` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100)
          OR (`total due at the start of the 3 months` AT MOST 300 AND (NOT `I made a payment in the period to reduce them`)))

-- s 185LC(3): a designated 6-month arrears default occurs at the test time if "(a) ... (i) before the test time, one or more payments
-- ... became due and payable ...; (ii) at no time during the 6-month period ending immediately before the test time were any
-- obligations in respect of those payments discharged; or (b) ... (i) at the test time, the obligations created by the debt agreement
-- have not been discharged; (ii) the last of those obligations should have been discharged at a time 6 months before the test time".
-- Months are whole months; "at a time 6 months before" is read as "6 months or more before" (inference).
@export Have I committed a designated 6-month arrears default (s 185LC(3))?
GIVEN `a payment had fallen due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any payment under the agreement has fallen due
      `months since I paid anything towards those payments` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since you last paid anything towards the payments that had fallen due
      `I have finished all my obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have discharged every obligation under the agreement
      `months since my last obligation fell due` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since your last obligation should have been discharged (0 if it is not yet due)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed a designated 6-month arrears default` IF
        (`a payment had fallen due` AND `months since I paid anything towards those payments` AT LEAST 6)
    OR  ((NOT `I have finished all my obligations`) AND `months since my last obligation fell due` AT LEAST 6)

-- s 185LC(1): the administrator "must notify, in writing, the Official Receiver ... within 10 business days". s 185QA(1): if the
-- administrator notifies and "the Official Receiver is satisfied that the designated 6-month arrears default has occurred", the
-- Official Receiver "must (c) declare in writing that the agreement is terminated; and (d) record the declaration on the National
-- Personal Insolvency Index". (2): terminated "when the declaration is recorded". s 185R: "A debt agreement is terminated if the
-- debtor becomes a bankrupt." Termination under s 185QA is itself an act of bankruptcy (s 40(1)(hd)).
@export Is my debt agreement terminated (ss 185QA, 185R)?
GIVEN `the administrator notified a designated 6-month arrears default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your administrator has told the Official Receiver of a designated 6-month arrears default
      `the Official Receiver is satisfied it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver is satisfied the default occurred
      `the declaration is recorded on the Index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver's declaration of termination has been recorded on the Index
      `I have become a bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have become a bankrupt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my debt agreement terminated` IF
        `I have become a bankrupt`
    OR  (    `the administrator notified a designated 6-month arrears default`
         AND `the Official Receiver is satisfied it occurred`
         AND `the declaration is recorded on the Index`)

@export Must the Official Receiver declare my debt agreement terminated (s 185QA(1))?
GIVEN `the administrator notified a designated 6-month arrears default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your administrator has told the Official Receiver of a designated 6-month arrears default
      `the Official Receiver is satisfied it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Official Receiver is satisfied the default occurred
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Official Receiver terminate my agreement` IF
    `the administrator notified a designated 6-month arrears default` AND `the Official Receiver is satisfied it occurred`

§§ `185M(1D)-(1DB) -- how far a variation may extend my payments`

-- s 185M(1D): a proposal to vary "must not seek to vary the agreement so that the agreement would provide for the debtor to make
-- payments ... after: (a) 3 years beginning on the day the agreement was made; or (b) if subsection (1DA) or (1DB) applies -- 5
-- years". (1DA): s 185C(2AB) applied to the debtor when the proposal was given. (1DB): the administrator certifies reasonable grounds
-- to believe "(i) that the debtor has suffered a substantial change in circumstances after the agreement was made that was not
-- foreseen ...; and (ii) that the debtor is not likely to be able to discharge the obligations ... because of that change"; and "(b)
-- the proposal does not increase the total of the payments".
@export If my debt agreement is varied, what is the longest, in years, my payments may then run (s 185M(1D))?
GIVEN `the home rule applied when I gave the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 185C(2AB) (your home) applied to you when you gave the original proposal
      `the administrator certifies an unforeseen substantial change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your administrator certifies an unforeseen substantial change in your circumstances that means you cannot keep up
      `the variation does not increase the total payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the variation leaves the total you must pay the same or lower
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years may a variation let my payments run` IS
    IF     `the home rule applied when I gave the proposal`
        OR (`the administrator certifies an unforeseen substantial change` AND `the variation does not increase the total payments`)
    THEN 5
    ELSE 3

§§ `185M(1E) -- how much a variation may ask me to pay`

-- s 185M(1E): if "(a) subsection 185C(2AB) did not apply to the debtor at the time (the proposal time) the relevant debt
-- agreement proposal was given" and "(b) a person did not give a certificate under paragraph 185C(4C)(b)", the proposal to vary
-- "must not seek to vary the agreement so that the amount worked out using the following formula (expressed as a percentage)
-- exceeds the percentage in effect under an instrument under subsection 185C(4B) at the proposal time". The formula, transcribed
-- in C1966A00033.formulas.md:
--     (Total of the payments that the debtor would be required to make under the agreement (as proposed to be varied)
--        + Low income debtor amount (within the meaning of section 185C) at the proposal time)
--     / The debtor's after tax income (within the meaning of section 185C) in the year beginning at the proposal time
@export May a proposed variation of my debt agreement ask me to pay this much (s 185M(1E))?
GIVEN `the home rule applied when I gave the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 185C(2AB) (your home) applied to you when you gave the original proposal
      `a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proposed administrator gave a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate with the original proposal
      `total payments as varied` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the payments you would be required to make under the agreement as proposed to be varied, in dollars
      `low income debtor amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The low income debtor amount at the original proposal time, in dollars
      `after tax income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your after tax income in the year beginning at the original proposal time, in dollars
      `the Minister's percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 185C(4B) percentage in effect at the original proposal time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the variation ask me to pay this much` IF
        `the home rule applied when I gave the proposal`
    OR  `a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate was given`
    OR  (NOT `Do my payments exceed the Minister's percentage` `total payments as varied` `low income debtor amount` `after tax income` `the Minister's percentage`)

§§ `185N, 185NA, 153(2) -- the end of my agreement and my release`

-- s 185N(1): "A debt agreement ends when all the obligations that it created have been discharged, unless the agreement has been
-- terminated earlier under section 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R." (2): the debtor "is entitled to any property that was subject to the
-- debt agreement but that was not required by the agreement to be distributed to creditors" (Example: Rhea sells her boat and car
-- for $16,000, pays her creditors the $15,000 required, and keeps $1,000). (3): the Official Receiver "must give the debtor a
-- certificate". (5): the administrator notifies the Official Receiver within 5 business days.
@export Has my debt agreement ended on completion (s 185N(1))?
GIVEN `I have discharged all my obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have done everything the agreement required
      `it was terminated earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement was terminated earlier under s 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my debt agreement ended` IF
    `I have discharged all my obligations` AND (NOT `it was terminated earlier`)

@export When my debt agreement ends, how much of the property it covered do I keep (s 185N(2))?
GIVEN `realised from the property` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property dealt with under the agreement brought in, in dollars
      `required to be distributed` IS A NUMBER @desc What the agreement required to be paid to creditors from it, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I keep` IS
    IF `realised from the property` GREATER THAN `required to be distributed`
    THEN `realised from the property` MINUS `required to be distributed`
    ELSE 0

-- s 185NA(1): when the agreement ends under s 185N(1), "the debtor is released from provable debts from which the debtor would have
-- been released if the debtor had been discharged from bankruptcy immediately after the acceptance of the relevant debt agreement
-- proposal for processing was recorded". (2): the release "ceases to operate if the debt agreement is declared void by the Court".
-- (3): it does not release a joint debtor or a guarantor.
-- s 153(2): discharge does not release (b) "a debt incurred by means of fraud" or (c) "subject to any order of the Court made under
-- subsection (2A)", a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order. s 153 Note: a pecuniary penalty order is not
-- provable (s 82(3A)). A proceeds of crime liability is treated as not released on that note (inference).
@export When my debt agreement ends, am I released from this debt (s 185NA)?
GIVEN `the debt` IS A `Debt kind` @desc The kind of debt
      `my agreement ended on completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement ended under s 185N(1) by your completing it
      `my agreement was declared void` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has declared the agreement void
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I released from the debt` IF
        `my agreement ended on completion`
    AND (NOT `my agreement was declared void`)
    AND CONSIDER `the debt`
        WHEN `an ordinary provable debt` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Does my release also release someone who owes the debt with me, or my guarantor (s 185NA(3))?
GIVEN `I was released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were released from the debt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my co-debtor or guarantor released` IF FALSE

§§ `Bankruptcy Regulations 2021 ss 82, 83 -- how long it stays on the Index`

-- Regs s 82(1): if a debt agreement "ends under section 185N", the Official Receiver "must remove all information relating to the debt
-- agreement from the Index within 1 month after the later of the following days: (a) 5 years after the day on which the debt
-- agreement was made; (b) the day on which the debt agreement ends". (2): if terminated under s 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R -- the later
-- of 5 years after it was made and "2 years after the day on which the debt agreement is terminated". (3): if declared wholly void
-- under s 185U -- the later of 5 years after it was made and "2 years after the day on which the order is made".
-- Regs s 83: information about a proposal that is withdrawn, not accepted, cancelled or lapses is removed "within 1 year after the
-- day on which any of the following occurs".
-- The answer is the day from which the month runs; removal must be done within 1 month after it.
DECLARE `How my agreement finished` IS ONE OF
    `it ended on completion under s 185N`
    `it was terminated under s 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R`
    `it was declared wholly void under s 185U`

@export From what day does the one month run within which my debt agreement must come off the National Personal Insolvency Index (Regulations s 82)?
GIVEN `how it finished` IS A `How my agreement finished` @desc How the agreement came to an end
      `the day it was made` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the agreement was made (entered on the Index), as YYYYMMDD
      `the day it finished` IS A NUMBER @desc The day it ended, was terminated, or was declared void, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `From when must my agreement come off the Index` IS
    CONSIDER `how it finished`
    WHEN `it ended on completion under s 185N` THEN
        `the higher of` (`the same day years later` `the day it was made` 5) `the day it finished`
    OTHERWISE
        `the higher of` (`the same day years later` `the day it was made` 5) (`the same day years later` `the day it finished` 2)

@export If my proposal does not become an agreement, by what day must it come off the National Personal Insolvency Index (Regulations s 83)?
GIVEN `the day it was withdrawn, rejected, cancelled or lapsed` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the proposal was withdrawn, not accepted, had its acceptance for processing cancelled, or lapsed, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By when must my proposal come off the Index` IS
    `the same day years later` `the day it was withdrawn, rejected, cancelled or lapsed` 1
